window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b358-4e1f7bdd9022a31d.json"]={sha256:"4e1f7bdd9022a31dcae9befafa75a1645a52842da3e0486ec390154e8209a7de",value:{"id":"b358","title":"鐵路橋軌相互作用分析","titleEn":"Rail–bridge interaction analysis","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"鐵路橋軌相互作用分析以「橋梁溫伸制動位移與鋼軌約束」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。橋梁與連續鋼軌透過扣件和支承交換縱向作用，橋梁溫度、制動以及支承布置會改變鋼軌附加力，不能把橋與軌各自分析後忽略相容。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops bridge thermal movement braking displacement and rail restraint through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. Bridges and continuous rails exchange longitudinal action through fastenings and supports; temperature, braking and bearing layout alter rail force, so separate analyses cannot omit compatibility. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-track","subcategoryTitle":"軌道與土建工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Track and civil engineering","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-track","learningTags":["rail","rail-track","track"],"architectureFamily":"rail-track","architectureNodes":[["橋梁溫度","Bridge temperature"],["橋梁支承","Bridge bearings"],["縱向扣件","Longitudinal fastenings"],["連續鋼軌","Continuous rails"],["橋端位移","Bridge-end movement"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-track","labels":["橋梁溫度","橋梁支承","縱向扣件","連續鋼軌","橋端位移"],"labelsEn":["Bridge temperature","Bridge bearings","Longitudinal fastenings","Continuous rails","Bridge-end movement"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=26.4 mm。模型邊界：均溫自由伸縮；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm；y=bridge-rail=15 mm。只把 bridge 增加百分之十，y=17 mm。模型邊界：同方向共同基準；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=26.4 mm. Boundary: Uniform-temperature free expansion; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm; y=bridge-rail=15 mm. Increasing only bridge with a ten-percent increase gives y=17 mm. Boundary: Shared datum and direction; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b358-v16-s1","title":"橋梁自由熱伸長與橋軌相對位移","titleEn":"Bridge free thermal movement & Relative rail-bridge movement","description":"本階段聚焦「橋梁自由熱伸長」與「橋軌相對位移」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bridge free thermal movement\" and \"Relative rail-bridge movement\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b358-v16-01","title":"橋梁自由熱伸長：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bridge free thermal movement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「橋梁自由熱伸長」如何影響鐵路橋軌相互作用分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bridge free thermal movement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail–bridge interaction analysis”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"自由端位移受有效伸縮長度而非總橋長控制。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 26.4 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均溫自由伸縮。使用固定支承位置與端部位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；固定點判錯會錯估位移方向，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「橋梁自由熱伸長」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Free-end movement depends on effective expansion length rather than total bridge length. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 26.4 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform-temperature free expansion. Use fixed-bearing location and endpoint movement as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bridge free thermal movement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：固定點判錯會錯估位移方向」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「橋梁自由熱伸長」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bridge free thermal movement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-01-k1","title":"橋梁自由熱伸長","titleEn":"Bridge free thermal movement","text":"自由端位移受有效伸縮長度而非總橋長控制。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 26.4 mm。","textEn":"Free-end movement depends on effective expansion length rather than total bridge length. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：固定點判錯會錯估位移方向 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橋梁自由熱伸長」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bridge free thermal movement\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：固定點判錯會錯估位移方向","自由端位移受有效伸縮長度而非總橋長控制。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：量測基準不同會產生假相對位移"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction.","Free-end movement depends on effective expansion length rather than total bridge length.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different datums create false relative movement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"自由端位移受有效伸縮長度而非總橋長控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Free-end movement depends on effective expansion length rather than total bridge length. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b358-v16-02","title":"橋梁自由熱伸長：定量估算","titleEn":"Bridge free thermal movement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橋梁自由熱伸長」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bridge free thermal movement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=26.4 mm。模型邊界：均溫自由伸縮；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=26.4 mm. Boundary: Uniform-temperature free expansion; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以固定支承位置與端部位移區分模型與觀察，先用梁溫計與端部位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use fixed-bearing location and endpoint movement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=26.4 mm。模型邊界：均溫自由伸縮；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=26.4 mm. Boundary: Uniform-temperature free expansion; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橋梁自由熱伸長」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bridge free thermal movement\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K；y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=80 m, dT=25 K; y=alpha*L*dT*1000=24 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b358-v16-03","title":"橋梁自由熱伸長：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bridge free thermal movement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橋梁自由熱伸長」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bridge free thermal movement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以固定支承位置與端部位移區分模型與觀察，先用梁溫計與端部位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「橋梁自由熱伸長」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use fixed-bearing location and endpoint movement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using girder thermometers and endpoint gauges, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Bridge free thermal movement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「橋梁自由熱伸長」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均溫自由伸縮如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由固定點判錯會錯估位移方向造成偏離的合成觀察，以固定支承位置與端部位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Bridge free thermal movement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform-temperature free expansion. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction. Explain which evidence in fixed-bearing location and endpoint movement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：固定點判錯會錯估位移方向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以固定支承位置與端部位移區分模型與觀察，先用梁溫計與端部位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「橋梁自由熱伸長」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use fixed-bearing location and endpoint movement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using girder thermometers and endpoint gauges, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Bridge free thermal movement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「橋梁自由熱伸長」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均溫自由伸縮如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由固定點判錯會錯估位移方向造成偏離的合成觀察，以固定支承位置與端部位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Bridge free thermal movement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform-temperature free expansion. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction. Explain which evidence in fixed-bearing location and endpoint movement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橋梁自由熱伸長」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bridge free thermal movement\"?","options":["本單元以固定支承位置與端部位移區分模型與觀察，先用梁溫計與端部位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程"],"optionsEn":["Use fixed-bearing location and endpoint movement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以固定支承位置與端部位移區分模型與觀察，先用梁溫計與端部位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use fixed-bearing location and endpoint movement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b358-v16-04","title":"橋梁自由熱伸長：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bridge free thermal movement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橋梁自由熱伸長」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bridge free thermal movement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"固定點判錯會錯估位移方向。這個失效與「橋梁自由熱伸長」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查固定支承位置與端部位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction. This failure and a measurement bias in Bridge free thermal movement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check fixed-bearing location and endpoint movement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用固定支承位置與端部位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；固定點判錯會錯估位移方向，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：固定點判錯會錯估位移方向」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"固定點判錯會錯估位移方向。這個失效與「橋梁自由熱伸長」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查固定支承位置與端部位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction. This failure and a measurement bias in Bridge free thermal movement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check fixed-bearing location and endpoint movement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橋梁自由熱伸長」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bridge free thermal movement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","固定點判錯會錯估位移方向。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：量測基準不同會產生假相對位移"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different datums create false relative movement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"固定點判錯會錯估位移方向。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b358-v16-05","title":"橋軌相對位移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Relative rail-bridge movement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「橋軌相對位移」如何影響鐵路橋軌相互作用分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Relative rail-bridge movement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail–bridge interaction analysis”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"扣件受的是橋軌相對位移而非橋梁絕對位移。本模型把 bridge 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 17 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。同方向共同基準。使用同位置橋軌雙位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；量測基準不同會產生假相對位移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「橋軌相對位移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Fastenings respond to relative bridge-rail movement rather than absolute bridge displacement. In this model, bridge is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 17 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Shared datum and direction. Use paired bridge and rail movement at one location as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Different datums create false relative movement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Relative rail-bridge movement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm；y=bridge-rail=15 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm; y=bridge-rail=15 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：量測基準不同會產生假相對位移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different datums create false relative movement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「橋軌相對位移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Relative rail-bridge movement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-05-k1","title":"橋軌相對位移","titleEn":"Relative rail-bridge movement","text":"扣件受的是橋軌相對位移而非橋梁絕對位移。本模型把 bridge 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 17 mm。","textEn":"Fastenings respond to relative bridge-rail movement rather than absolute bridge displacement. In this model, bridge is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：量測基準不同會產生假相對位移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different datums create false relative movement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橋軌相對位移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Relative rail-bridge movement\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：量測基準不同會產生假相對位移","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：滑移後不能延用線性剛度","扣件受的是橋軌相對位移而非橋梁絕對位移。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different datums create false relative movement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip.","Fastenings respond to relative bridge-rail movement rather than absolute bridge displacement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"扣件受的是橋軌相對位移而非橋梁絕對位移。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Fastenings respond to relative bridge-rail movement rather than absolute bridge displacement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b358-v16-06","title":"橋軌相對位移：定量估算","titleEn":"Relative rail-bridge movement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橋軌相對位移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Relative rail-bridge movement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm；y=bridge-rail=15 mm。只把 bridge 增加百分之十，y=17 mm。模型邊界：同方向共同基準；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm; y=bridge-rail=15 mm. Increasing only bridge with a ten-percent increase gives y=17 mm. Boundary: Shared datum and direction; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以同位置橋軌雙位移區分模型與觀察，先用雙通道位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use paired bridge and rail movement at one location to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm；y=bridge-rail=15 mm。只把 bridge 增加百分之十，y=17 mm。模型邊界：同方向共同基準；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm; y=bridge-rail=15 mm. Increasing only bridge with a ten-percent increase gives y=17 mm. Boundary: Shared datum and direction; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橋軌相對位移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Relative rail-bridge movement\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm；y=bridge-rail=15 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm; y=bridge-rail=15 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm；y=bridge-rail=15 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: bridge=20 mm, rail=5 mm; y=bridge-rail=15 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b358-v16-07","title":"橋軌相對位移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Relative rail-bridge movement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橋軌相對位移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Relative rail-bridge movement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以同位置橋軌雙位移區分模型與觀察，先用雙通道位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「橋軌相對位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use paired bridge and rail movement at one location to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using two-channel displacement gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Relative rail-bridge movement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「橋軌相對位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出同方向共同基準如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由量測基準不同會產生假相對位移造成偏離的合成觀察，以同位置橋軌雙位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Relative rail-bridge movement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Shared datum and direction. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Different datums create false relative movement. Explain which evidence in paired bridge and rail movement at one location distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：量測基準不同會產生假相對位移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Different datums create false relative movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以同位置橋軌雙位移區分模型與觀察，先用雙通道位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「橋軌相對位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use paired bridge and rail movement at one location to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using two-channel displacement gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Relative rail-bridge movement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「橋軌相對位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出同方向共同基準如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由量測基準不同會產生假相對位移造成偏離的合成觀察，以同位置橋軌雙位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Relative rail-bridge movement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Shared datum and direction. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Different datums create false relative movement. Explain which evidence in paired bridge and rail movement at one location distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橋軌相對位移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Relative rail-bridge movement\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以同位置橋軌雙位移區分模型與觀察，先用雙通道位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use paired bridge and rail movement at one location to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以同位置橋軌雙位移區分模型與觀察，先用雙通道位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use paired bridge and rail movement at one location to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b358-v16-08","title":"橋軌相對位移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Relative rail-bridge movement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橋軌相對位移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Relative rail-bridge movement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"量測基準不同會產生假相對位移。這個失效與「橋軌相對位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查同位置橋軌雙位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Different datums create false relative movement. This failure and a measurement bias in Relative rail-bridge movement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check paired bridge and rail movement at one location rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用同位置橋軌雙位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；量測基準不同會產生假相對位移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Different datums create false relative movement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：量測基準不同會產生假相對位移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different datums create false relative movement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"量測基準不同會產生假相對位移。這個失效與「橋軌相對位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查同位置橋軌雙位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Different datums create false relative movement. This failure and a measurement bias in Relative rail-bridge movement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check paired bridge and rail movement at one location rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橋軌相對位移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Relative rail-bridge movement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：滑移後不能延用線性剛度","量測基準不同會產生假相對位移。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip.","Different datums create false relative movement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測基準不同會產生假相對位移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Different datums create false relative movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b358-v16-s2","title":"縱向彈性分力與制動平均分布","titleEn":"Longitudinal elastic force & Mean braking distribution","description":"本階段聚焦「縱向彈性分力」與「制動平均分布」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Longitudinal elastic force\" and \"Mean braking distribution\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b358-v16-09","title":"縱向彈性分力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Longitudinal elastic force: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「縱向彈性分力」如何影響鐵路橋軌相互作用分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Longitudinal elastic force” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail–bridge interaction analysis”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"線性區相對位移經扣件剛度轉成縱向力。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 49.5 kN。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。單扣件預滑移區。使用相對位移與扣件力作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；滑移後不能延用線性剛度，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「縱向彈性分力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Within the linear range, relative movement becomes force through fastening stiffness. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 49.5 kN. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. One fastening before slip. Use relative movement and fastening force as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Longitudinal elastic force” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=15 kN/mm, d=3 mm；y=k*d=45 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=15 kN/mm, d=3 mm; y=k*d=45 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：滑移後不能延用線性剛度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「縱向彈性分力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Longitudinal elastic force”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-09-k1","title":"縱向彈性分力","titleEn":"Longitudinal elastic force","text":"線性區相對位移經扣件剛度轉成縱向力。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 49.5 kN。","textEn":"Within the linear range, relative movement becomes force through fastening stiffness. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：滑移後不能延用線性剛度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「縱向彈性分力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Longitudinal elastic force\" is correct?","options":["線性區相對位移經扣件剛度轉成縱向力。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：滑移後不能延用線性剛度","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值"],"optionsEn":["Within the linear range, relative movement becomes force through fastening stiffness.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"線性區相對位移經扣件剛度轉成縱向力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Within the linear range, relative movement becomes force through fastening stiffness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b358-v16-10","title":"縱向彈性分力：定量估算","titleEn":"Longitudinal elastic force: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「縱向彈性分力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Longitudinal elastic force” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=15 kN/mm, d=3 mm；y=k*d=45 kN。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=49.5 kN。模型邊界：單扣件預滑移區；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=15 kN/mm, d=3 mm; y=k*d=45 kN. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=49.5 kN. Boundary: One fastening before slip; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以相對位移與扣件力區分模型與觀察，先用低載扣件模型建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use relative movement and fastening force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=15 kN/mm, d=3 mm；y=k*d=45 kN。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=49.5 kN。模型邊界：單扣件預滑移區；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=15 kN/mm, d=3 mm; y=k*d=45 kN. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=49.5 kN. Boundary: One fastening before slip; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「縱向彈性分力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Longitudinal elastic force\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=15 kN/mm, d=3 mm；y=k*d=45 kN。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=15 kN/mm, d=3 mm; y=k*d=45 kN.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=15 kN/mm, d=3 mm；y=k*d=45 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=15 kN/mm, d=3 mm; y=k*d=45 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b358-v16-11","title":"縱向彈性分力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Longitudinal elastic force: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「縱向彈性分力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Longitudinal elastic force” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以相對位移與扣件力區分模型與觀察，先用低載扣件模型建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「縱向彈性分力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use relative movement and fastening force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load fastening model, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Longitudinal elastic force. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「縱向彈性分力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出單扣件預滑移區如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由滑移後不能延用線性剛度造成偏離的合成觀察，以相對位移與扣件力說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Longitudinal elastic force, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: One fastening before slip. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip. Explain which evidence in relative movement and fastening force distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：滑移後不能延用線性剛度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以相對位移與扣件力區分模型與觀察，先用低載扣件模型建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「縱向彈性分力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use relative movement and fastening force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load fastening model, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Longitudinal elastic force. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「縱向彈性分力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出單扣件預滑移區如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由滑移後不能延用線性剛度造成偏離的合成觀察，以相對位移與扣件力說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Longitudinal elastic force, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: One fastening before slip. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip. Explain which evidence in relative movement and fastening force distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「縱向彈性分力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Longitudinal elastic force\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力","本單元以相對位移與扣件力區分模型與觀察，先用低載扣件模型建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Changing one support alters force in the other.","Use relative movement and fastening force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以相對位移與扣件力區分模型與觀察，先用低載扣件模型建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use relative movement and fastening force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b358-v16-12","title":"縱向彈性分力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Longitudinal elastic force: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「縱向彈性分力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Longitudinal elastic force” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"滑移後不能延用線性剛度。這個失效與「縱向彈性分力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查相對位移與扣件力，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip. This failure and a measurement bias in Longitudinal elastic force can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check relative movement and fastening force rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用相對位移與扣件力作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；滑移後不能延用線性剛度，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：滑移後不能延用線性剛度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"滑移後不能延用線性剛度。這個失效與「縱向彈性分力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查相對位移與扣件力，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip. This failure and a measurement bias in Longitudinal elastic force can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check relative movement and fastening force rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「縱向彈性分力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Longitudinal elastic force\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["滑移後不能延用線性剛度。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值"],"optionsEn":["Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"滑移後不能延用線性剛度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b358-v16-13","title":"制動平均分布：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mean braking distribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「制動平均分布」如何影響鐵路橋軌相互作用分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mean braking distribution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail–bridge interaction analysis”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"總制動力均布是簡化假設，真實載入跟列車位置移動。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 4.4 kN/m。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。已知有效受力長度。使用列車位置與縱向載入作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「制動平均分布」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Uniform total braking force is a simplification; actual loading moves with train position. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 4.4 kN/m. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Known effective loaded length. Use train position and longitudinal loading as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Uniform loading can miss local peaks; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mean braking distribution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=800 kN, L=200 m；y=F/L=4 kN/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=800 kN, L=200 m; y=F/L=4 kN/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「制動平均分布」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mean braking distribution”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-13-k1","title":"制動平均分布","titleEn":"Mean braking distribution","text":"總制動力均布是簡化假設，真實載入跟列車位置移動。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 4.4 kN/m。","textEn":"Uniform total braking force is a simplification; actual loading moves with train position. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「制動平均分布」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mean braking distribution\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值","總制動力均布是簡化假設，真實載入跟列車位置移動。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks.","Uniform total braking force is a simplification; actual loading moves with train position.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action."],"answer":1,"explanation":"總制動力均布是簡化假設，真實載入跟列車位置移動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Uniform total braking force is a simplification; actual loading moves with train position. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b358-v16-14","title":"制動平均分布：定量估算","titleEn":"Mean braking distribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「制動平均分布」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mean braking distribution” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=800 kN, L=200 m；y=F/L=4 kN/m。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=4.4 kN/m。模型邊界：已知有效受力長度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=800 kN, L=200 m; y=F/L=4 kN/m. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=4.4 kN/m. Boundary: Known effective loaded length; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以列車位置與縱向載入區分模型與觀察，先用合成列車位置與力建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use train position and longitudinal loading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=800 kN, L=200 m；y=F/L=4 kN/m。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=4.4 kN/m。模型邊界：已知有效受力長度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=800 kN, L=200 m; y=F/L=4 kN/m. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=4.4 kN/m. Boundary: Known effective loaded length; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「制動平均分布」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mean braking distribution\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=800 kN, L=200 m；y=F/L=4 kN/m。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=800 kN, L=200 m; y=F/L=4 kN/m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=800 kN, L=200 m；y=F/L=4 kN/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=800 kN, L=200 m; y=F/L=4 kN/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b358-v16-15","title":"制動平均分布：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mean braking distribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「制動平均分布」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mean braking distribution” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以列車位置與縱向載入區分模型與觀察，先用合成列車位置與力建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「制動平均分布」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use train position and longitudinal loading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic train positions and forces, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Mean braking distribution. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「制動平均分布」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出已知有效受力長度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值造成偏離的合成觀察，以列車位置與縱向載入說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Mean braking distribution, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Known effective loaded length. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks. Explain which evidence in train position and longitudinal loading distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uniform loading can miss local peaks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以列車位置與縱向載入區分模型與觀察，先用合成列車位置與力建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「制動平均分布」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use train position and longitudinal loading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic train positions and forces, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Mean braking distribution. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「制動平均分布」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出已知有效受力長度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值造成偏離的合成觀察，以列車位置與縱向載入說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Mean braking distribution, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Known effective loaded length. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks. Explain which evidence in train position and longitudinal loading distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「制動平均分布」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mean braking distribution\"?","options":["本單元以列車位置與縱向載入區分模型與觀察，先用合成列車位置與力建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：固定點判錯會錯估位移方向"],"optionsEn":["Use train position and longitudinal loading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以列車位置與縱向載入區分模型與觀察，先用合成列車位置與力建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use train position and longitudinal loading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b358-v16-16","title":"制動平均分布：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mean braking distribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「制動平均分布」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mean braking distribution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值。這個失效與「制動平均分布」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查列車位置與縱向載入，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uniform loading can miss local peaks. This failure and a measurement bias in Mean braking distribution can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check train position and longitudinal loading rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用列車位置與縱向載入作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Uniform loading can miss local peaks; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值。這個失效與「制動平均分布」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查列車位置與縱向載入，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Uniform loading can miss local peaks. This failure and a measurement bias in Mean braking distribution can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check train position and longitudinal loading rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「制動平均分布」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mean braking distribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Uniform loading can miss local peaks.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action."],"answer":1,"explanation":"均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uniform loading can miss local peaks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b358-v16-s3","title":"支承縱向位移與鋼軌附加應力","titleEn":"Longitudinal bearing displacement & Additional rail stress","description":"本階段聚焦「支承縱向位移」與「鋼軌附加應力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Longitudinal bearing displacement\" and \"Additional rail stress\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b358-v16-17","title":"支承縱向位移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Longitudinal bearing displacement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「支承縱向位移」如何影響鐵路橋軌相互作用分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Longitudinal bearing displacement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail–bridge interaction analysis”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"支承柔度把縱向作用轉為橋梁移動。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3.3 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。單一線性支承。使用支承力位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支承縱向位移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bearing flexibility converts longitudinal action into bridge movement. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 3.3 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. One linear bearing. Use bearing force-displacement as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Longitudinal bearing displacement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, k=100 kN/mm；y=F/k=3 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, k=100 kN/mm; y=F/k=3 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支承縱向位移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Longitudinal bearing displacement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-17-k1","title":"支承縱向位移","titleEn":"Longitudinal bearing displacement","text":"支承柔度把縱向作用轉為橋梁移動。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3.3 mm。","textEn":"Bearing flexibility converts longitudinal action into bridge movement. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支承縱向位移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Longitudinal bearing displacement\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合","支承柔度把縱向作用轉為橋梁移動。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination.","Bearing flexibility converts longitudinal action into bridge movement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"支承柔度把縱向作用轉為橋梁移動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bearing flexibility converts longitudinal action into bridge movement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b358-v16-18","title":"支承縱向位移：定量估算","titleEn":"Longitudinal bearing displacement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支承縱向位移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Longitudinal bearing displacement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, k=100 kN/mm；y=F/k=3 mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=3.3 mm。模型邊界：單一線性支承；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, k=100 kN/mm; y=F/k=3 mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.3 mm. Boundary: One linear bearing; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以支承力位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型支承荷重元建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use bearing force-displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, k=100 kN/mm；y=F/k=3 mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=3.3 mm。模型邊界：單一線性支承；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, k=100 kN/mm; y=F/k=3 mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.3 mm. Boundary: One linear bearing; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支承縱向位移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Longitudinal bearing displacement\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, k=100 kN/mm；y=F/k=3 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, k=100 kN/mm; y=F/k=3 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Changing one support alters force in the other."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, k=100 kN/mm；y=F/k=3 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, k=100 kN/mm; y=F/k=3 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b358-v16-19","title":"支承縱向位移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Longitudinal bearing displacement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支承縱向位移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Longitudinal bearing displacement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以支承力位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型支承荷重元建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「支承縱向位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use bearing force-displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model bearing load cell, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Longitudinal bearing displacement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「支承縱向位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出單一線性支承如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用造成偏離的合成觀察，以支承力位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Longitudinal bearing displacement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: One linear bearing. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action. Explain which evidence in bearing force-displacement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以支承力位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型支承荷重元建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「支承縱向位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use bearing force-displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model bearing load cell, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Longitudinal bearing displacement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「支承縱向位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出單一線性支承如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用造成偏離的合成觀察，以支承力位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Longitudinal bearing displacement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: One linear bearing. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action. Explain which evidence in bearing force-displacement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支承縱向位移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Longitudinal bearing displacement\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以支承力位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型支承荷重元建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：量測基準不同會產生假相對位移"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use bearing force-displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different datums create false relative movement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以支承力位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型支承荷重元建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use bearing force-displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b358-v16-20","title":"支承縱向位移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Longitudinal bearing displacement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支承縱向位移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Longitudinal bearing displacement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用。這個失效與「支承縱向位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查支承力位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action. This failure and a measurement bias in Longitudinal bearing displacement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check bearing force-displacement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用支承力位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用。這個失效與「支承縱向位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查支承力位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action. This failure and a measurement bias in Longitudinal bearing displacement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check bearing force-displacement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支承縱向位移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Longitudinal bearing displacement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合","支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination.","A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action."],"answer":2,"explanation":"支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b358-v16-21","title":"鋼軌附加應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Additional rail stress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「鋼軌附加應力」如何影響鐵路橋軌相互作用分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Additional rail stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail–bridge interaction analysis”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"附加軸力需與既有熱應力依相容模型組合。本模型把 N 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 28.9474 MPa。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均勻軸應力。使用鋼軌應變與溫度補償作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鋼軌附加應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Additional axial force must be combined with existing thermal stress consistently. In this model, N is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 28.9474 MPa. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform axial stress. Use rail strain with temperature compensation as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Additional rail stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：N=200 kN, A=7600 mm2；y=N*1000/A=26.3158 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: N=200 kN, A=7600 mm2; y=N*1000/A=26.3158 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鋼軌附加應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Additional rail stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-21-k1","title":"鋼軌附加應力","titleEn":"Additional rail stress","text":"附加軸力需與既有熱應力依相容模型組合。本模型把 N 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 28.9474 MPa。","textEn":"Additional axial force must be combined with existing thermal stress consistently. In this model, N is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼軌附加應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Additional rail stress\" is correct?","options":["附加軸力需與既有熱應力依相容模型組合。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移"],"optionsEn":["Additional axial force must be combined with existing thermal stress consistently.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"附加軸力需與既有熱應力依相容模型組合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Additional axial force must be combined with existing thermal stress consistently. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b358-v16-22","title":"鋼軌附加應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Additional rail stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼軌附加應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Additional rail stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：N=200 kN, A=7600 mm2；y=N*1000/A=26.3158 MPa。只把 N 增加百分之十，y=28.9474 MPa。模型邊界：均勻軸應力；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: N=200 kN, A=7600 mm2; y=N*1000/A=26.3158 MPa. Increasing only N with a ten-percent increase gives y=28.9474 MPa. Boundary: Uniform axial stress; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以鋼軌應變與溫度補償區分模型與觀察，先用溫補應變計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use rail strain with temperature compensation to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：N=200 kN, A=7600 mm2；y=N*1000/A=26.3158 MPa。只把 N 增加百分之十，y=28.9474 MPa。模型邊界：均勻軸應力；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: N=200 kN, A=7600 mm2; y=N*1000/A=26.3158 MPa. Increasing only N with a ten-percent increase gives y=28.9474 MPa. Boundary: Uniform axial stress; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼軌附加應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Additional rail stress\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：N=200 kN, A=7600 mm2；y=N*1000/A=26.3158 MPa。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：固定點判錯會錯估位移方向"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: N=200 kN, A=7600 mm2; y=N*1000/A=26.3158 MPa.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：N=200 kN, A=7600 mm2；y=N*1000/A=26.3158 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: N=200 kN, A=7600 mm2; y=N*1000/A=26.3158 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b358-v16-23","title":"鋼軌附加應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Additional rail stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼軌附加應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Additional rail stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以鋼軌應變與溫度補償區分模型與觀察，先用溫補應變計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「鋼軌附加應力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use rail strain with temperature compensation to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using temperature-compensated strain gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Additional rail stress. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「鋼軌附加應力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻軸應力如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合造成偏離的合成觀察，以鋼軌應變與溫度補償說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Additional rail stress, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform axial stress. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination. Explain which evidence in rail strain with temperature compensation distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以鋼軌應變與溫度補償區分模型與觀察，先用溫補應變計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「鋼軌附加應力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use rail strain with temperature compensation to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using temperature-compensated strain gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Additional rail stress. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「鋼軌附加應力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻軸應力如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合造成偏離的合成觀察，以鋼軌應變與溫度補償說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Additional rail stress, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform axial stress. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination. Explain which evidence in rail strain with temperature compensation distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼軌附加應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Additional rail stress\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：滑移後不能延用線性剛度","本單元以鋼軌應變與溫度補償區分模型與觀察，先用溫補應變計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip.","Use rail strain with temperature compensation to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以鋼軌應變與溫度補償區分模型與觀察，先用溫補應變計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use rail strain with temperature compensation to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b358-v16-24","title":"鋼軌附加應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Additional rail stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼軌附加應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Additional rail stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合。這個失效與「鋼軌附加應力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查鋼軌應變與溫度補償，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination. This failure and a measurement bias in Additional rail stress can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail strain with temperature compensation rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用鋼軌應變與溫度補償作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合。這個失效與「鋼軌附加應力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查鋼軌應變與溫度補償，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination. This failure and a measurement bias in Additional rail stress can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail strain with temperature compensation rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼軌附加應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Additional rail stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移"],"optionsEn":["Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b358-v16-s4","title":"橋端轉角位移與伸縮裝置餘量","titleEn":"Bridge-end rotation movement & Expansion-device reserve","description":"本階段聚焦「橋端轉角位移」與「伸縮裝置餘量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bridge-end rotation movement\" and \"Expansion-device reserve\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b358-v16-25","title":"橋端轉角位移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bridge-end rotation movement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「橋端轉角位移」如何影響鐵路橋軌相互作用分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bridge-end rotation movement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail–bridge interaction analysis”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"梁端轉角透過高度差產生附加縱向位移。本模型把 theta 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.65 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。小轉角剛體投影。使用梁端轉角與軌面高度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「橋端轉角位移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"End rotation creates longitudinal movement through vertical offset. In this model, theta is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 1.65 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Small-angle rigid-body projection. Use end rotation and rail-level offset as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bridge-end rotation movement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：theta=0.001 rad, h=1.5 m；y=theta*h*1000=1.5 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: theta=0.001 rad, h=1.5 m; y=theta*h*1000=1.5 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「橋端轉角位移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bridge-end rotation movement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-25-k1","title":"橋端轉角位移","titleEn":"Bridge-end rotation movement","text":"梁端轉角透過高度差產生附加縱向位移。本模型把 theta 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.65 mm。","textEn":"End rotation creates longitudinal movement through vertical offset. In this model, theta is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橋端轉角位移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bridge-end rotation movement\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移","梁端轉角透過高度差產生附加縱向位移。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement.","End rotation creates longitudinal movement through vertical offset.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"梁端轉角透過高度差產生附加縱向位移。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"End rotation creates longitudinal movement through vertical offset. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b358-v16-26","title":"橋端轉角位移：定量估算","titleEn":"Bridge-end rotation movement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橋端轉角位移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bridge-end rotation movement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：theta=0.001 rad, h=1.5 m；y=theta*h*1000=1.5 mm。只把 theta 增加百分之十，y=1.65 mm。模型邊界：小轉角剛體投影；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: theta=0.001 rad, h=1.5 m; y=theta*h*1000=1.5 mm. Increasing only theta with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.65 mm. Boundary: Small-angle rigid-body projection; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以梁端轉角與軌面高度區分模型與觀察，先用傾角計與位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use end rotation and rail-level offset to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：theta=0.001 rad, h=1.5 m；y=theta*h*1000=1.5 mm。只把 theta 增加百分之十，y=1.65 mm。模型邊界：小轉角剛體投影；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: theta=0.001 rad, h=1.5 m; y=theta*h*1000=1.5 mm. Increasing only theta with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.65 mm. Boundary: Small-angle rigid-body projection; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橋端轉角位移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bridge-end rotation movement\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：量測基準不同會產生假相對位移","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：theta=0.001 rad, h=1.5 m；y=theta*h*1000=1.5 mm。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Changing one support alters force in the other.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different datums create false relative movement.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: theta=0.001 rad, h=1.5 m; y=theta*h*1000=1.5 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：theta=0.001 rad, h=1.5 m；y=theta*h*1000=1.5 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: theta=0.001 rad, h=1.5 m; y=theta*h*1000=1.5 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b358-v16-27","title":"橋端轉角位移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bridge-end rotation movement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橋端轉角位移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bridge-end rotation movement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以梁端轉角與軌面高度區分模型與觀察，先用傾角計與位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「橋端轉角位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use end rotation and rail-level offset to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using inclinometer and displacement gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Bridge-end rotation movement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「橋端轉角位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出小轉角剛體投影如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移造成偏離的合成觀察，以梁端轉角與軌面高度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Bridge-end rotation movement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Small-angle rigid-body projection. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement. Explain which evidence in end rotation and rail-level offset distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以梁端轉角與軌面高度區分模型與觀察，先用傾角計與位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「橋端轉角位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use end rotation and rail-level offset to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using inclinometer and displacement gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Bridge-end rotation movement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「橋端轉角位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出小轉角剛體投影如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移造成偏離的合成觀察，以梁端轉角與軌面高度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Bridge-end rotation movement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Small-angle rigid-body projection. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement. Explain which evidence in end rotation and rail-level offset distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橋端轉角位移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bridge-end rotation movement\"?","options":["本單元以梁端轉角與軌面高度區分模型與觀察，先用傾角計與位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值"],"optionsEn":["Use end rotation and rail-level offset to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以梁端轉角與軌面高度區分模型與觀察，先用傾角計與位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use end rotation and rail-level offset to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b358-v16-28","title":"橋端轉角位移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bridge-end rotation movement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橋端轉角位移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bridge-end rotation movement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移。這個失效與「橋端轉角位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查梁端轉角與軌面高度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement. This failure and a measurement bias in Bridge-end rotation movement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check end rotation and rail-level offset rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用梁端轉角與軌面高度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移。這個失效與「橋端轉角位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查梁端轉角與軌面高度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement. This failure and a measurement bias in Bridge-end rotation movement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check end rotation and rail-level offset rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橋端轉角位移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bridge-end rotation movement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b358-v16-29","title":"伸縮裝置餘量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Expansion-device reserve: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「伸縮裝置餘量」如何影響鐵路橋軌相互作用分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Expansion-device reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail–bridge interaction analysis”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"位移預算需保留溫度及其他同時作用。本模型把 range 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 50 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。同方向保守代數合成。使用裝置位置與工況作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「伸縮裝置餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Movement budget must retain temperature and concurrent actions. In this model, range is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 50 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Conservative same-direction algebraic combination. Use device position and load case as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Expansion-device reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：range=100 mm, thermal=50 mm, brake=10 mm；y=range-thermal-brake=40 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: range=100 mm, thermal=50 mm, brake=10 mm; y=range-thermal-brake=40 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「伸縮裝置餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Expansion-device reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-29-k1","title":"伸縮裝置餘量","titleEn":"Expansion-device reserve","text":"位移預算需保留溫度及其他同時作用。本模型把 range 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 50 mm。","textEn":"Movement budget must retain temperature and concurrent actions. In this model, range is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「伸縮裝置餘量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Expansion-device reserve\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲","位移預算需保留溫度及其他同時作用。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending.","Movement budget must retain temperature and concurrent actions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"位移預算需保留溫度及其他同時作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Movement budget must retain temperature and concurrent actions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b358-v16-30","title":"伸縮裝置餘量：定量估算","titleEn":"Expansion-device reserve: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「伸縮裝置餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Expansion-device reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：range=100 mm, thermal=50 mm, brake=10 mm；y=range-thermal-brake=40 mm。只把 range 增加百分之十，y=50 mm。模型邊界：同方向保守代數合成；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: range=100 mm, thermal=50 mm, brake=10 mm; y=range-thermal-brake=40 mm. Increasing only range with a ten-percent increase gives y=50 mm. Boundary: Conservative same-direction algebraic combination; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以裝置位置與工況區分模型與觀察，先用裝置行程量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use device position and load case to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：range=100 mm, thermal=50 mm, brake=10 mm；y=range-thermal-brake=40 mm。只把 range 增加百分之十，y=50 mm。模型邊界：同方向保守代數合成；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: range=100 mm, thermal=50 mm, brake=10 mm; y=range-thermal-brake=40 mm. Increasing only range with a ten-percent increase gives y=50 mm. Boundary: Conservative same-direction algebraic combination; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「伸縮裝置餘量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Expansion-device reserve\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：range=100 mm, thermal=50 mm, brake=10 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：固定點判錯會錯估位移方向","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：滑移後不能延用線性剛度"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: range=100 mm, thermal=50 mm, brake=10 mm; y=range-thermal-brake=40 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：range=100 mm, thermal=50 mm, brake=10 mm；y=range-thermal-brake=40 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: range=100 mm, thermal=50 mm, brake=10 mm; y=range-thermal-brake=40 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b358-v16-31","title":"伸縮裝置餘量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Expansion-device reserve: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「伸縮裝置餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Expansion-device reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以裝置位置與工況區分模型與觀察，先用裝置行程量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「伸縮裝置餘量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use device position and load case to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using device travel measurements, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Expansion-device reserve. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「伸縮裝置餘量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出同方向保守代數合成如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程造成偏離的合成觀察，以裝置位置與工況說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Expansion-device reserve, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Conservative same-direction algebraic combination. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel. Explain which evidence in device position and load case distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以裝置位置與工況區分模型與觀察，先用裝置行程量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「伸縮裝置餘量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use device position and load case to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using device travel measurements, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Expansion-device reserve. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「伸縮裝置餘量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出同方向保守代數合成如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程造成偏離的合成觀察，以裝置位置與工況說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Expansion-device reserve, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Conservative same-direction algebraic combination. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel. Explain which evidence in device position and load case distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「伸縮裝置餘量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Expansion-device reserve\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以裝置位置與工況區分模型與觀察，先用裝置行程量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use device position and load case to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以裝置位置與工況區分模型與觀察，先用裝置行程量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use device position and load case to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b358-v16-32","title":"伸縮裝置餘量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Expansion-device reserve: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「伸縮裝置餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Expansion-device reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程。這個失效與「伸縮裝置餘量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查裝置位置與工況，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel. This failure and a measurement bias in Expansion-device reserve can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check device position and load case rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用裝置位置與工況作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程。這個失效與「伸縮裝置餘量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查裝置位置與工況，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel. This failure and a measurement bias in Expansion-device reserve can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check device position and load case rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「伸縮裝置餘量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Expansion-device reserve\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲","中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending.","An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel."],"answer":2,"explanation":"中性位置偏移會耗掉單側行程。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An offset neutral position consumes one-sided travel. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b358-v16-s5","title":"溫差梯度曲率與相容反力分配","titleEn":"Thermal-gradient curvature & Compatible reaction sharing","description":"本階段聚焦「溫差梯度曲率」與「相容反力分配」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Thermal-gradient curvature\" and \"Compatible reaction sharing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b358-v16-33","title":"溫差梯度曲率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal-gradient curvature: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「溫差梯度曲率」如何影響鐵路橋軌相互作用分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thermal-gradient curvature” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail–bridge interaction analysis”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"梁上下溫差可造成彎曲而非僅縱向伸長。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 6.6e-05 1/m。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。線性溫差自由曲率。使用上下表面溫度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「溫差梯度曲率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Top-bottom temperature difference creates bending, not just longitudinal expansion. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 6.6e-05 1/m. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Free curvature under a linear thermal gradient. Use top and bottom surface temperatures as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thermal-gradient curvature” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, dT=10 K, h=2 m；y=alpha*dT/h=6e-05 1/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, dT=10 K, h=2 m; y=alpha*dT/h=6e-05 1/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「溫差梯度曲率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thermal-gradient curvature”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-33-k1","title":"溫差梯度曲率","titleEn":"Thermal-gradient curvature","text":"梁上下溫差可造成彎曲而非僅縱向伸長。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 6.6e-05 1/m。","textEn":"Top-bottom temperature difference creates bending, not just longitudinal expansion. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫差梯度曲率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal-gradient curvature\" is correct?","options":["梁上下溫差可造成彎曲而非僅縱向伸長。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力"],"optionsEn":["Top-bottom temperature difference creates bending, not just longitudinal expansion.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Changing one support alters force in the other."],"answer":0,"explanation":"梁上下溫差可造成彎曲而非僅縱向伸長。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Top-bottom temperature difference creates bending, not just longitudinal expansion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b358-v16-34","title":"溫差梯度曲率：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal-gradient curvature: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「溫差梯度曲率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thermal-gradient curvature” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, dT=10 K, h=2 m；y=alpha*dT/h=6e-05 1/m。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=6.6e-05 1/m。模型邊界：線性溫差自由曲率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, dT=10 K, h=2 m; y=alpha*dT/h=6e-05 1/m. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=6.6e-05 1/m. Boundary: Free curvature under a linear thermal gradient; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以上下表面溫度區分模型與觀察，先用多高度溫度探頭建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use top and bottom surface temperatures to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, dT=10 K, h=2 m；y=alpha*dT/h=6e-05 1/m。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=6.6e-05 1/m。模型邊界：線性溫差自由曲率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, dT=10 K, h=2 m; y=alpha*dT/h=6e-05 1/m. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=6.6e-05 1/m. Boundary: Free curvature under a linear thermal gradient; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「溫差梯度曲率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal-gradient curvature\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：量測基準不同會產生假相對位移","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, dT=10 K, h=2 m；y=alpha*dT/h=6e-05 1/m。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均布假設可能漏掉局部峰值"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different datums create false relative movement.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, dT=10 K, h=2 m; y=alpha*dT/h=6e-05 1/m.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform loading can miss local peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, dT=10 K, h=2 m；y=alpha*dT/h=6e-05 1/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, dT=10 K, h=2 m; y=alpha*dT/h=6e-05 1/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b358-v16-35","title":"溫差梯度曲率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal-gradient curvature: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「溫差梯度曲率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thermal-gradient curvature” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以上下表面溫度區分模型與觀察，先用多高度溫度探頭建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「溫差梯度曲率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use top and bottom surface temperatures to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using temperature probes at multiple heights, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Thermal-gradient curvature. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「溫差梯度曲率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出線性溫差自由曲率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲造成偏離的合成觀察，以上下表面溫度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Thermal-gradient curvature, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Free curvature under a linear thermal gradient. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending. Explain which evidence in top and bottom surface temperatures distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以上下表面溫度區分模型與觀察，先用多高度溫度探頭建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「溫差梯度曲率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use top and bottom surface temperatures to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using temperature probes at multiple heights, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Thermal-gradient curvature. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「溫差梯度曲率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出線性溫差自由曲率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲造成偏離的合成觀察，以上下表面溫度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Thermal-gradient curvature, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Free curvature under a linear thermal gradient. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending. Explain which evidence in top and bottom surface temperatures distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「溫差梯度曲率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal-gradient curvature\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：直接相加互斥工況會產生不實組合","本單元以上下表面溫度區分模型與觀察，先用多高度溫度探頭建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Adding mutually exclusive cases creates an unreal combination.","Use top and bottom surface temperatures to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以上下表面溫度區分模型與觀察，先用多高度溫度探頭建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use top and bottom surface temperatures to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b358-v16-36","title":"溫差梯度曲率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal-gradient curvature: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「溫差梯度曲率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thermal-gradient curvature” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲。這個失效與「溫差梯度曲率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查上下表面溫度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending. This failure and a measurement bias in Thermal-gradient curvature can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check top and bottom surface temperatures rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用上下表面溫度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲。這個失效與「溫差梯度曲率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查上下表面溫度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending. This failure and a measurement bias in Thermal-gradient curvature can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check top and bottom surface temperatures rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫差梯度曲率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal-gradient curvature\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力"],"optionsEn":["Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Changing one support alters force in the other."],"answer":0,"explanation":"均溫模型會漏掉熱彎曲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uniform-temperature models miss thermal bending. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b358-v16-37","title":"相容反力分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Compatible reaction sharing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「相容反力分配」如何影響鐵路橋軌相互作用分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Compatible reaction sharing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail–bridge interaction analysis”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平行支承同位移而依剛度分力。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 440 kN。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。兩個平行線性支承。使用各支承反力與共同位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「相容反力分配」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Parallel supports share displacement and divide force by stiffness. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 440 kN. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Two parallel linear supports. Use support reactions and common displacement as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Changing one support alters force in the other; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Compatible reaction sharing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=600 kN, k1=80 kN/mm, k2=40 kN/mm；y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=400 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=600 kN, k1=80 kN/mm, k2=40 kN/mm; y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=400 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Changing one support alters force in the other.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「相容反力分配」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Compatible reaction sharing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-37-k1","title":"相容反力分配","titleEn":"Compatible reaction sharing","text":"平行支承同位移而依剛度分力。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 440 kN。","textEn":"Parallel supports share displacement and divide force by stiffness. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Changing one support alters force in the other. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「相容反力分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Compatible reaction sharing\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力","平行支承同位移而依剛度分力。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：固定點判錯會錯估位移方向"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Changing one support alters force in the other.","Parallel supports share displacement and divide force by stiffness.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平行支承同位移而依剛度分力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Parallel supports share displacement and divide force by stiffness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b358-v16-38","title":"相容反力分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Compatible reaction sharing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「相容反力分配」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Compatible reaction sharing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=600 kN, k1=80 kN/mm, k2=40 kN/mm；y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=400 kN。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=440 kN。模型邊界：兩個平行線性支承；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=600 kN, k1=80 kN/mm, k2=40 kN/mm; y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=400 kN. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=440 kN. Boundary: Two parallel linear supports; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以各支承反力與共同位移區分模型與觀察，先用雙荷重元與位移基準建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use support reactions and common displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=600 kN, k1=80 kN/mm, k2=40 kN/mm；y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=400 kN。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=440 kN。模型邊界：兩個平行線性支承；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=600 kN, k1=80 kN/mm, k2=40 kN/mm; y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=400 kN. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=440 kN. Boundary: Two parallel linear supports; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「相容反力分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Compatible reaction sharing\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：滑移後不能延用線性剛度","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承卡死會重新分配橋軌作用","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=600 kN, k1=80 kN/mm, k2=40 kN/mm；y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=400 kN。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear stiffness cannot be extended beyond slip.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A seized bearing redistributes bridge-rail action.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=600 kN, k1=80 kN/mm, k2=40 kN/mm; y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=400 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=600 kN, k1=80 kN/mm, k2=40 kN/mm；y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=400 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=600 kN, k1=80 kN/mm, k2=40 kN/mm; y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=400 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b358-v16-39","title":"相容反力分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Compatible reaction sharing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「相容反力分配」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Compatible reaction sharing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以各支承反力與共同位移區分模型與觀察，先用雙荷重元與位移基準建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「相容反力分配」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use support reactions and common displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paired load cells and displacement datum, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Compatible reaction sharing. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「相容反力分配」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩個平行線性支承如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力造成偏離的合成觀察，以各支承反力與共同位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Compatible reaction sharing, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Two parallel linear supports. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Changing one support alters force in the other. Explain which evidence in support reactions and common displacement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Changing one support alters force in the other. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以各支承反力與共同位移區分模型與觀察，先用雙荷重元與位移基準建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「相容反力分配」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use support reactions and common displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paired load cells and displacement datum, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Compatible reaction sharing. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「相容反力分配」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩個平行線性支承如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力造成偏離的合成觀察，以各支承反力與共同位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Compatible reaction sharing, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Two parallel linear supports. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Changing one support alters force in the other. Explain which evidence in support reactions and common displacement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「相容反力分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Compatible reaction sharing\"?","options":["本單元以各支承反力與共同位移區分模型與觀察，先用雙荷重元與位移基準建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略梁高會漏掉轉角誘發位移"],"optionsEn":["Use support reactions and common displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring girder depth misses rotation-induced movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以各支承反力與共同位移區分模型與觀察，先用雙荷重元與位移基準建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use support reactions and common displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b358-v16-40","title":"相容反力分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Compatible reaction sharing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b358-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「相容反力分配」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Compatible reaction sharing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力。這個失效與「相容反力分配」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各支承反力與共同位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Changing one support alters force in the other. This failure and a measurement bias in Compatible reaction sharing can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check support reactions and common displacement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用各支承反力與共同位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Changing one support alters force in the other; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Changing one support alters force in the other.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b358-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力。這個失效與「相容反力分配」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各支承反力與共同位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Changing one support alters force in the other. This failure and a measurement bias in Compatible reaction sharing can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check support reactions and common displacement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b358-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「相容反力分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Compatible reaction sharing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：固定點判錯會錯估位移方向"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Changing one support alters force in the other.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: An incorrect fixed point misidentifies movement direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一支承剛度變化會改變其他支承力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Changing one support alters force in the other. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b358-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b358-en.svg"}};
